  "$doc": "The curated zh sentence corpus (issue #20). Hand-written cleanroom Traditional sentences over the closed world — no sentence is copied from any corpus, textbook, or dictionary. Every sliver word appears in at least one sentence (machine-checked by tools/validate_assets.py); `cut` is the pinned AS/CKIP-standard unit sequence (the reference the segmenter votes are normalized against, per design §6.7 — the noun+ordinal 星期|一, V|O 喝|茶, and neg+V 不|好 conventions follow the stub's committed pinned standard). This corpus is: (a) the g2pW base-reading agreement input (gate leg 2), (b) the multi-segmenter vote input (gate leg 3), (c) the g2pW drift-job corpus (.github/workflows/drift-g2pw.yml), and (d) a gold-pass item block (AC7). C9 carrier sentences are generated separately by the builder from sliver/contexts-grammar.json.",
